# Seed a valid persisted SoftAp config before the framework starts.
#
# TCL's TctWifiManagerEx.getTctDefaultSoftApConfiguration() builds the default
# soft AP config from the def_framework_softap_* / def_framework_wifi_ap_passward
# resources. Those live on TCL's per-product vendor overlay, which this QEMU
# vendor partition does not ship, so the passphrase comes out empty and
# SoftApConfiguration.Builder.setPassphrase() throws in system_server's
# WifiHandlerThread, killing the whole framework every boot.
#
# WifiApConfigStore.getApConfiguration() returns the persisted config when one
# exists, so seeding it here avoids the broken default path entirely.
#
# init cannot exec /system/bin/sh (there is no init -> shell domain transition),
# so this uses init's own builtins instead of a shell script. This init's copy
# takes only <src> <dst>, so ownership and mode are set separately.
# The copy overwrites any runtime edits each boot; that is acceptable for this VM
# and keeps the framework from ever reaching TCL's default builder.
on post-fs-data
    mkdir /data/misc/apexdata/com.android.wifi 0771 root system
    copy /vendor/etc/tebox/WifiConfigStoreSoftAp.xml /data/misc/apexdata/com.android.wifi/WifiConfigStoreSoftAp.xml
    chown system system /data/misc/apexdata/com.android.wifi/WifiConfigStoreSoftAp.xml
    chmod 0600 /data/misc/apexdata/com.android.wifi/WifiConfigStoreSoftAp.xml
    restorecon /data/misc/apexdata/com.android.wifi/WifiConfigStoreSoftAp.xml
